# Deployment Manual: FastAPI & Telegram Bot on Shopla Server

This guide is designed for an AI Coding Agent to understand and implement a deployment workflow for a FastAPI + Telegram Bot project on the existing server.

## 1. Server Environment Overview

- **IP Address:** `158.220.100.58`
- **SSH User:** `root`
- **Main OS:** Ubuntu/Linux
- **Proxy:** Nginx (Reverse Proxy)
- **Containerization:** Docker & Docker Compose

### Existing Port Mappings:
| Service | Local Port | Domain |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Frontend (Shopla) | 3000 | `shopla.uz`, `*.shopla.uz` |
| Backend API | 8001 | `api.shopla.uz` |
| Admin Panel | 8002 | `admin.shopla.uz` |
| MinIO | 9000 | `/minio/` path |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Your new FastAPI project must use a unique port (e.g., **8003** or **8010**) to avoid conflicts.

